{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3054","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3054","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3054\",\"parent_revision\":\"b97b5be773066ecc2e71fc6346de923c524d249e13419a910610965c14ce98fe\",\"root_revision\":\"b97b5be773066ecc2e71fc6346de923c524d249e13419a910610965c14ce98fe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe plugin's documentation does not describe its own structure. There is no component map. Eight code packages exist (`agent_profile`, `backlog_core`, `dh_core`, `dispatch_schema`, `hooks`, `progressive_markdown`, `sam_schema`, `scripts`); exactly one of them has an `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Nothing states what each package owns, what it consumes, which packages are near-duplicates of each other, or where the authoritative detail for each lives.\\n\\nThe consequence is measurable and was demonstrated repeatedly in a single session: an agent starting work reads whichever package it lands in, treats that package's behaviour as the system's behaviour, and generalises incorrectly. Specific failures observed, each traceable to a missing line of a component map:\\n\\n- The markdown engine (`progressive_markdown`) was not discovered until late, by accident, after a search in a sibling directory failed. Work was nearly started to build a capability that already existed and was fully tested.\\n- Two distinct markdown handling paths \u2014 storage-key resolution and navigation indexing \u2014 were conflated, producing a confident and wrong claim that the system handled only two heading levels.\\n- A duplicate test file was created because only one of the plugin's six test roots was searched.\\n- A new architecture document was committed with no deduplication against two sibling documents it overlapped, no cross-references, and no entry in any discovery index.\\n- Two committed documents were found to state directly contradictory behaviour, discovered only incidentally.\\n\\nThis item covers the systematic pass. It is deliberately sequenced after the targeted markdown-consumption architecture work so that the smaller, well-understood surface is settled first and can serve as the pattern.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Every code package in the plugin has an architecture description covering role, owns, consumes, consumed-by, and detail location\\n- [ ] Near-collisions between modules and concepts carry explicit distinction notes\\n- [ ] Concepts and glossary consolidated to one definition each, with other references linking rather than restating\\n- [ ] Shared root path and naming convention defined and documented\\n- [ ] Drift audit complete: every plugin document fact-checked against code, workflow, and prose behaviour\\n- [ ] Drift review chart produced, supporting all three adjudication outcomes per entry, and reviewed\\n- [ ] Cross-reference table produced identifying every multi-document topic and its duplicate sources\\n- [ ] The resulting material is reachable from the plugin's discovery index, not orphaned\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs **an agent or contributor working anywhere in the development-harness plugin**, I want **an authoritative per-module architecture description, a consolidated concept glossary, and a verified record of where documentation and behaviour disagree** so that **I can find the right component and the right detail without inferring the system's shape from whichever file I happened to open first**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, 2026-08-20 \u2014 architecture drift investigation across the backlog and markdown-handling subsystems\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 documentation drift is actively producing incorrect agent work, with repeated instances observed in a single session\\n- **Sequencing**: Deferred. Begins after the targeted markdown-consumption architecture description is settled; that smaller surface serves as the pattern for this broader pass.\\n- **Related**: #3050 (ADR identifiers referenced but undefined \u2014 a subset of the same problem); #3052 (tool documentation omits implemented parameters); PR #3053 (targeted integration of three overlapping documents, done reactively rather than systematically)\\n\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Required Deliverables\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### 1. Per-module architecture and relationships\\n\\nFor every code package in the plugin, a description covering: the module's role in one sentence; what it owns; what it consumes and from where; what consumes it; and where its authoritative detail lives.\\n\\nEach near-collision between modules or concepts carries an explicit distinction note stating that the two are not the same and how to tell them apart. The observed failure mode is not \\\"could not find it\\\" but \\\"found something adjacent and assumed it was the thing\\\" \u2014 the distinction notes exist to stop that specifically.\\n\\n### 2. Authoritative concept consolidation and glossary\\n\\nOne definition per concept, stated once, in a known location. Every other document referencing that concept links to the definition rather than restating it.\\n\\n### 3. Structure design at a shared root path\\n\\nA defined home for this material, with the arrangement and naming convention documented, so that a new module's documentation has an obvious correct location and an agent has an obvious correct place to look.\\n\\n### 4. Documentation-versus-behaviour drift audit\\n\\nEvery existing document in the plugin is fact-checked against what the plugin actually does \u2014 code, workflow, and prose instruction alike. For each discrepancy found, record: the document and the specific claim; the actual observed behaviour; and the nature of the difference.\\n\\nThe output is a review chart listing every discrepancy for adjudication. Each entry must support three outcomes:\\n\\n- the documentation is correct and the implementation must change;\\n- the implementation is correct and the documentation must change;\\n- neither matches the desired architecture, and a written direction is supplied for what the correct state is.\\n\\nThe chart is produced for review. Entries are not resolved unilaterally.\\n\\n### 5. Cross-reference and duplicate-source table\\n\\nA table identifying every topic described in more than one document, showing which documents cover it and where they agree, diverge, or contradict. This is the deduplication work list: each row resolves to one authoritative source with the others reduced to links.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Architecture Baseline\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIntended behaviour and component ownership are recorded in two documents:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md` \u2014 normative requirements R1\u2013R8 and the required flow\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md` \u2014 package map, ownership boundaries, and do-not-confuse-with notes\\n\\nBoth are under review in PR #3053 (integration and deduplication against existing docs) and PR #3056 (component map, contract scope binding, review-round amendments).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Gap Items Bridging Current State To The Architecture\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Item | Gap |\\n|---|---|\\n| #3057 | Default item-read path hand-builds its index and pagination instead of using the engine |\\n| #3058 | Plan, task, and artifact reads are unbounded against the harness response cap |\\n| #3059 | Navigation and pagination are reimplemented on top of the engine rather than used from it |\\n| #3060 | Runtime hints steer agents toward full-content retrieval |\\n| #3061 | Sections and artifacts are separate lookups rather than one inventory |\\n| #3062 | Paginated content has no content identity, so pages re-collect and can span versions |\\n| #3063 | The CLI cannot reach address-based navigation |\\n| #3064 | Agent instructions mandate full-item fetches the contract supersedes |\\n\\nRelated, filed separately: #3055 (registered artifacts whose content cannot be read) blocks #3061; #3050 (referenced ADRs with no definition documents); #2453 (agents hardcode section names with no route to a source of truth).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Sequencing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3057 requires the grooming validation gate to read section presence from the engine before the hand-built structures it currently depends on are removed.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6c10051c1609808cf9b44c3790031303ec837ccb713555a03adea4834f0b502b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPulb9g\"}"}